course: dictionary
lesson: 1867
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Cola is one of them. Its main meaning is a sweet, fizzy, brown drink. «A can of cola» means a drink you can open and pour.
explain: Cola can also mean a tall tropical tree. Its nuts were first used to give the drink its flavour, so the two meanings are linked. Look at the words around cola: if they mention bubbles, sugar or a can, the drink is meant. If they mention a forest or a hot island, the tree is meant.
explain: Context also shows you how a word is used. «Diet cola» is the same kind of drink with sweeteners instead of sugar, so the word diet changes the meaning a little. Cola is also part of phrases like «cola bottle» and «cola sweets».
explain: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Cola is a noun. Its plural is colas, as in «two colas, please».
fact: Cola is a sweet, fizzy, brown soft drink, usually containing caffeine.
fact: The cola tree is a tropical tree whose nuts were first used for the flavour.
fact: Cola is carbonated, which means carbon dioxide gas is dissolved in it, so it fizzes.
fact: Cola is a treat, not an everyday drink, because it is sugary and acidic, and these can harm your teeth.
exercise: «Drop Mentos into a bottle of diet cola and a fountain shoots up.» In this sentence, what is cola? | A tropical tree | A glass bottle | A kind of sweet | *A fizzy brown drink
exercise: «A can of normal cola sinks, and a can of diet cola floats.» Why does normal cola sink? | It is made from a tree | It is colder than diet cola | It has more bubbles than diet cola | *Its sugar makes it a little heavier
exercise: Ella reads «The cola tree grew in the hot forest» and says cola means a fizzy drink. What does cola mean here? | *A tropical tree | A fizzy drink | A bottle with a lid | A sweet you suck
test: «One can of ordinary cola has a lot of sugar; diet drinks use sweeteners.» What does ordinary mean in this sentence? | Very old | *Normal, usual | Bright and shiny | Tiny
test: «Diet cola makes a bigger fountain because its ingredients help bubbles form even faster.» What does fountain mean? | A kind of tree | *A spray that shoots up | A bottle with a lid | A large cup
exam: Why is cola a treat and not an everyday drink? | Because it is too cold to drink often | *Because it is sugary and acidic, which can harm teeth | Because it only grows in hot forests | Because it has no flavour at all
